Template: homelab-api/db/host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: PostgreSQL database host:
 Enter the hostname or IP address of the PostgreSQL server homelab-api
 should use for authentication (it reads a dovecot.users table) and its
 own api.* schema.
 .
 If you don't have an existing PostgreSQL server, leave this as
 "localhost" — if connectivity fails you will be offered the option to
 install and configure one automatically on this machine.

Template: homelab-api/db/port
Type: string
Default: 5432
Description: PostgreSQL database port:

Template: homelab-api/db/name
Type: string
Default: mailserver
Description: PostgreSQL database name:

Template: homelab-api/db/user
Type: string
Default: dovecot_user
Description: PostgreSQL database username:

Template: homelab-api/db/password
Type: password
Description: PostgreSQL database password:
 Enter the password for the above database user.

Template: homelab-api/db/connect_failed
Type: note
Description: Could not connect to the specified database
 homelab-api could not connect to PostgreSQL using the connection
 details you provided. You can continue and let this installer set up
 a local PostgreSQL server instead, or decline and fix
 /etc/homelab/api/config.yml by hand afterward.

Template: homelab-api/db/install_local
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Configure a local PostgreSQL server?
 homelab-api could not reach a PostgreSQL server at the address you
 provided. If the postgresql package is installed (or gets installed
 alongside homelab-api, which Recommends it), automatically create the
 database, role, schema, and a demo dovecot.users table homelab-api
 needs to run standalone?
 .
 Decline this if you plan to point homelab-api at an existing mail
 server's PostgreSQL database later and will configure it by hand.
